/E (Problem: Group smartphone sensor windows into meaningful clusters without using activity labels during training, and determine which clustering algorithm \(K-Means, DB- SCAN, or Hierarchical\) best recovers the structure of the six underlying human activities. Input: The UCI Human Activity Recognition Using Smartphones dataset \(training partition\), containing 7352 windows of 2.56 s each \(128 readings at 50 Hz\) recorded from waist-mounted smartphone accelerometers and gyroscopes, each described by 561 time- and frequency-domain features.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [12]
