/P 73 0 R
/E (Inference: K-Means with k = 2 splits the data almost exactly along the static/dynamic boundary seen in the ground-truth plot: one cluster covers the compact static region on the left of the PCA plot and the left group in t-SNE, and the other covers the dynamic activities on the right. The two clusters are clean and well separated in t-SNE, but the model cannot distinguish sitting from standing from laying, or the three walking types from each other, since these are merged into the two clusters.)
