377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Inference: The Ward dendrogram has a very tall final merge \(height around 380\) joining two main branches, followed by a second large merge \(height around 165\), which points to two dominant groups \(static and dynamic\) with further sub-structure below. The complete-linkage dendrogram is more compact \(final merge around 94\) with a smaller isolated branch. The average-linkage dendrogram has one very large branch plus a few small, late-merging branches, and the single-linkage dendrogram shows the typical chain- ing pattern: a staircase of merges at almost equal, low heights, where points are absorbed one by one into a growing cluster.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
