/E (How sensitive was K-Means to the choice of k? Quite sensitive. The silhouette)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (score dropped from 0.397 at k = 2 to 0.327 at k = 3 and to 0.163 at k = 4, and continued down to 0.083 at k = 8, so quality falls quickly once k exceeds the natural two-group structure. The WCSS curve, by contrast, decreases smoothly with no sharp elbow \(only a mild bend near k = 3\), so the elbow method alone would not give a decisive choice on this dataset and needs to be combined with the silhouette curve.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E <FEFF004400690064002000440042005300430041004E00200064006500740065006300740020006E006F0069007300650020006F007200200073006D0061006C006C00200063006C0075007300740065007200730020006500660066006500630074006900760065006C0079003F00200050006100720074006C0079002E00200057006900740068002003F50020003D>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (11.35 and minPts = 10 it flagged 1411 points \(19.2%\) as noise, mainly sparse, irregular windows in the dynamic region, and produced several very small clusters in addition to the two large ones. However, the results depended strongly on parameters: the number of clusters ranged from 18 to 1 and the noise from 171 to 1762 points across the 12 tested settings, and the small clusters do not correspond to individual activities. DBSCAN is therefore useful for identifying outlier windows but not for separating the six activities.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (How does linkage choice \(single/complete/Ward\) affect hierarchical clus-)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (tering? Very strongly. Ward linkage gave the best agreement with the true labels \(ARI 0.279, NMI 0.454\), complete linkage gave weaker agreement \(ARI 0.048, NMI 0.148\), and average and single linkage gave essentially no agreement \(ARI 0.000, NMI 0.003 and 0.002\). The single-linkage dendrogram shows the chaining effect \(points absorbed one by one into a growing cluster\), and the ARI and NMI values close to zero for single and average linkage indicate that the six-cluster cuts of these trees do not divide the data in a way related to the activities, most likely isolating a few outliers while leaving nearly all points in one cluster.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
